{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines","id":1198028,"title":"Talented Baselines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-21T10:28:49-07:00","id":1198028,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Talented Baselines","content":"Back in the Trinity Universe, there was something of a conflict among the developers as to the nature of daredevils. Bruce Baugh argued that daredevils were <i>paramorphs</i>, a third type of enhanced humanity that used subconscious probability manipulation to achieve feats of heroic action and unlikely coincidence. Meanwhile, Andrew Bates argued that daredevils were \u201cmerely\u201d exceptionally talented and fortunate people whose luck was just a genre convention, not an in-setting power; and that there was exactly one paramorph in the game, the \u201cunstuck in time\u201d Max Mercer.<br /> <br /> I admit to having a fondness for Andrews interpretation, and was hoping that Trinity Continuum would support it. They didn't. So Im providing this hack as a way of integrating the notion that daredevils are \u201ctalented baselines\u201d, and not paramorphs. <br /> <br /> That said, I'm backing off somewhat from the notion that the coincidences and lucky breaks that daredeils are surrounded by are just a genre convention. I'll stick with TC's notion of cross-time Flux being the source of the lucky breaks and related phenomena. The main change I'm making is that the subconscious manipulation of Flux isn't the realm of the paramorph, but rather something that anyone can do \u2014 although in general, only heroic and villainous types tap into that potential. In this hack, there are no Talents; instead, baseline characters have access to the abilities currently restricted to Talents. <br /> <br /> There is no Inspiration trait, and no Facets \u2014 although your choice of \u201cfavored Approach\u201d plays a similar role. Dramatic Editing is something done using Momentum, meaning that it isn't restricted by one's choice of Template (or lack thereof) but rather by one's role in the game: protagonists and similarly important characters have access to Momentum (and thus Dramatic Editing) while bit players and the like don't. I'm debating what to do about Gifts right now; either they're still a thing, or they get converted into Skill Tricks or Edges as appropriate. <br /> <br /> Another thing I'm debating is the inclusion of a \u201cMomentum surcharge\u201d for enhanced humans using abilities formerly the sole province of Talents: if you want a psion or Nova to engage in Dramatic Editing or to acquire and use a Gift, you can; but it will cost you more Momentum to do so. And you <i>don't</i> get to use Psi, Quantum, Taint, or whatever else to pay for these abilities. <br /> <br /> That's the basics of the idea here: Momentum instead of Inspiration, with a higher cost for those who have their own powers to rely on. I'll post more later; I just wanted to get the basics out there for now.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T10:56:58-07:00","id":1198035,"title":"","content":"As I'm firmly in the Bruce Baugh camp of paramorphs being a third group I wouldn't really use this. <br /> <br /> BUT at the same time the idea you present is intriguing, especially as part of say a core book only campaign in a world different from the base setting. <br /> <br /> I also like, in such a setting, the idea of dramatic editing being something any human with these talents could do. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I think it's nifty from a game mechanics sense, though I would never use it in the actual Trinity setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T12:02:55-07:00","id":1198061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198035#post1198035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I'm firmly in the Bruce Baugh camp of paramorphs being a third group I wouldn't really use this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the paramorph is very definitely a third type, even with this hack. The difference is that daredevils arent paramorphs. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198035#post1198035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BUT at the same time the idea you present is intriguing, especially as part of say a core book only campaign in a world different from the base setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>How different would it have to be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198035#post1198035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also like, in such a setting, the idea of dramatic editing being something any human with these talents could do.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I think it's nifty from a game mechanics sense, though I would never use it in the actual Trinity setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough; not every hack is for everyone, and this one is specifically intended to appeal to the \u201copposite camp\u201d from the one youre in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T13:26:20-07:00","id":1198090,"title":"","content":"My head canon was always sort of hybrid at least in the old timeline. Everyone was potentially a Daredevil it just needed a high amount of Z-rays/Flux for them to be able to do it(also humanity was the Lucky race because of this)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T14:51:13-07:00","id":1198132,"title":"","content":"Is this where I point out that I was complaining about the &quot;-morph&quot; terminology the other day and Bruce said he didn't really like it either?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23899-topher-gerkey","name":"Topher Gerkey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T16:45:55-07:00","id":1198164,"title":"","content":"If Talents aren't a special third group then what is stopping say a Psion or Aberrant from also becoming a Daredevil?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T19:42:53-07:00","id":1198214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198164#post1198164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Talents aren't a special third group then what is stopping say a Psion or Aberrant from also becoming a Daredevil?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The fact that Daredevils/Talents are under this model a complete abstraction and not a distinct thing in-setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T19:53:04-07:00","id":1198215,"title":"","content":"Psions and Aberrants aren't quite human anymore \u2014 Aberrants moreso than psions, but it applies to both. If you really want to say that they can't engage in Dramatic Editing, just say that their connection to Psi or Quantum hinders their ability to manipulate Flux. That can either justify the Momentum surcharge that I've been considering or an outright ban. I don't see the need to be quite that harsh (there's a place in both the superhero and sci-fi genres for serendipity); but that's me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:03:19-07:00","id":1198217,"title":"","content":"Yeah I assume Flux is incompatible with quantum and psi. But the fact Daredevils is a meta thing is consequential. I'm saying if Daredevils don't harness flux and are just super talented and a little lucky then being a Nova or Psion they could look at Talent Batman and think I'm smart and can do backflips so if I trained I should be able to achieve anything Talent Batman can achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:19:12-07:00","id":1198222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198217#post1198217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I assume Flux is incompatible with quantum and psi. But the fact Daredevils is a meta thing is consequential. I'm saying if Daredevils don't harness flux and are just super talented and a little lucky then being a Nova or Psion they could look at Talent Batman and think I'm smart and can do backflips so if I trained I should be able to achieve anything Talent Batman can achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The same thing that stops any of the superpowered Justice Leaguers from doing that? Theoretically nothing, but their awesomeness is already played out in their powers, they don't need the additional narrative contrivances Batman does so they don't get them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:21:33-07:00","id":1198223,"title":"","content":"I'm just saying in story reasons for NPCs and PCs alike rather then players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:41:04-07:00","id":1198232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198223#post1198223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just saying in story reasons for NPCs and PCs alike rather then players.</div> </div> </div> </div>... again... the fact that they're not a thing in setting. Psions and Novas can't choose to use Dramatic Editing or Gifts because Dramatic Editing and Gifts doesn't exist in-setting in this interpretation. They're just a mechanical abstraction to represent a baseline being lucky/brilliant/etc enough to hold their own with super-beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:45:18-07:00","id":1198235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198232#post1198232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... again... the fact that they're not a thing in setting. Psions and Novas can't choose to use Dramatic Editing or Gifts because Dramatic Editing and Gifts doesn't exist in-setting in this interpretation. They're just a mechanical abstraction to represent a baseline being lucky/brilliant/etc enough to hold their own with super-beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is what I am saying. Since its not a thing what is stopping someone from wanting to try to equal someone that is a Talent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T20:50:05-07:00","id":1198237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198217#post1198217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I assume Flux is incompatible with quantum and psi. But the fact Daredevils is a meta thing is consequential. I'm saying if Daredevils don't harness flux and are just super talented and a little lucky then being a Nova or Psion they could look at Talent Batman and think I'm smart and can do backflips so if I trained I should be able to achieve anything Talent Batman can achieve.</div> </div> </div> </div> Technically, if you're saying that daredevils don't harness Flux, you're not talking about this hack. But let's go with that for the sake of argument: if you're going with the notion that daredevils are lucky because the genre conventions say that they're lucky, then why are you expecting an in-story (i.e., less meta) explanation for why superhumans <i>aren't</i> as lucky? They aren't as lucky as the daredevils because the genre conventions <i>say</i> that they're not as lucky. <br /> <br /> As for training, psions and Aberrants tend to put their points into their powers, not their skills and paths. The psion isn't going to be the same kind of world-class martial artist as Batman because she's devoted much of her time developing her Psi instead. <br /> <br /> But again, this hack does <i>not</i> say that daredevils don't have access to Flux. It says that baselines <i>do</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-22-2018, 12:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T18:35:01-07:00","id":1198488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198214#post1198214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The fact that Daredevils/Talents are under this model a complete abstraction and not a distinct thing in-setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again I feel the need to say this.<br /> <br /> Daredevils ARE NOT Talents! Talents are Daredevil+ based on what we have been told by the Devs.<br /> This may change but my understanding is Talents are to Daredevils, what Mesmercists are to Psiads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T19:20:20-07:00","id":1198505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198488#post1198488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again I feel the need to say this.<br /> <br /> Daredevils ARE NOT Talents! Talents are Daredevil+ based on what we have been told by the Devs.<br /> This may change but my understanding is Talents are to Daredevils, what Mesmercists are to Psiads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna need you to quote your source for that. Everything I recall is that Talents are Daredevils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:02:42-07:00","id":1198520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198505#post1198505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gonna need you to quote your source for that. Everything I recall is that Talents are Daredevils.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he is confused because he assumes Talents to be equivalent to Psions and Novas. But Talents actually are a step behind them just like Mesmerists and Stalwarts and Daredevils, because they are Daredevils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:04:26-07:00","id":1198521,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's because in game both Psions and Talents are of the same tier. Though I don't truly consider that to be an indication of where a group lies on the spectrum of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T22:02:56-07:00","id":1198561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198488#post1198488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again I feel the need to say this.<br /> <br /> Daredevils ARE NOT Talents! Talents are Daredevil+ based on what we have been told by the Devs.<br /> This may change but my understanding is Talents are to Daredevils, what Mesmercists are to Psiads.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless we decide to change what daredevils are, I've been saying for years now that Talents are the modern name for what Adventure! called daredevils. They're the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T22:40:59-07:00","id":1198565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198488#post1198488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again I feel the need to say this.<br /> <br /> Daredevils ARE NOT Talents! Talents are Daredevil+ based on what we have been told by the Devs.<br /> This may change but my understanding is Talents are to Daredevils, what Mesmerists are to Psiads.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purposes of this topic, daredevils (lower-case d) are not Daredevils (capital D): that is, they're not a third type of enhanced human. They're baseline humans who are prone to taking risks and leading adventurous lives. They just happen to live in a reality where baseline humans can subconsciously manipulate Flux to cheat the odds \u2014 something with which daredevils have a lot of experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T08:27:44-07:00","id":1198672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1198520#post1198520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he is confused because he assumes Talents to be equivalent to Psions and Novas. But Talents actually are a step behind them just like Mesmerists and Stalwarts and Daredevils, because they are Daredevils.</div> </div> </div> </div>Talents aren\u2019t a step behind. Talents are Tier 2 with Psions, Psiads, and Superiors (artificially created eximorphs). Novas are Tier 3 with the Proxies and Max Mercer.<br /> <br /> If and how Mesmerists and Stalwarts fit into this remains to be seen. It\u2019s possible Mesmerists are just Psiads with era appropriate names for the low levels of the Modes they can buy. And Stalwarts may be balanced with Superiors the way Psiads are with Psions. We\u2019ll see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-23-2018, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T19:28:01-07:00","id":1454034,"title":"","content":"Just came across this little hack and I quite like it for a setting hack I'm putting together.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm in the camp (for my setting at least) that the &quot;Talents&quot; are like Jason Bourne, John Mcclane, Nick Fury, Bruce Wayne and so on in that &quot;Dramatic Editing&quot; is an out of game mechanic to explain their in-game awesomeness. There is no &quot;Flux&quot;, they're not reaching across timelines/probabilities - they're just that tough, smart, prepared, &amp; yes lucky.<br /> <br /> I think that &quot;Dramatic Editing&quot; is a great game mechanic in general and the use of Momentum actually makes ludonarrative sense - for every failure/drawback the characters encounter, they somehow make up for it in being well prepared, tough, or just generally &quot;bad ass&quot;. Their failures are just story elements that drive their inevitable future successes.<br /> <br /> The way I'd explain (out of game) that Psiads and low-level Novas don't get the same benefits is that they've already been lucky enough to get powers and so they need more failures to give them a non-powered solution to future problems. They've come to rely on their innate strengths so much they don't need to prepare as much (which is both a story &amp; real world trope). Think about how often Superman needs to pull out a conveniently pre-planned contingency compared to Batman. When Supes comes across an immovable obstacle, he just starts pounding on it harder. When Batman comes across the same obstacle, he's already conveniently researched the issue and created a gadget / plan to get around it. Supes might still need to pull out a Deus Ex Machina stye workaround, but he's got to fail more often with his powers before he reaches that point. Batman pretty much <b>relies</b> on his ability to just rewrite the plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T19:53:36-07:00","id":1454038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1454034#post1454034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they're just that tough, smart, prepared, &amp; yes lucky.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, part of the setting conceit of the Trinity Continuum is that this -- the whole probability manipulation thing -- is <i>how luck actually works</i>. Talents are just better at it than most, but it's not something they're consciously aware of. Like, if you can see a slightly wider range of colour than your friends, you may never notice, and it's not something you try to do, it just happens. There are people who live well into adulthood before finding out they're colourblind. After all, without the ability to compare, most of us are going to assume that our own experiences are universal.<br /> <br /> This is why I've long maintained that it's difficult to pin down who is and isn't a Talent: they're arguably not a Special Character Type in the way that psions and novas are. They're doing what every other human does subconsciously, they're just better at doing it. So the words &quot;flux&quot; and &quot;probability&quot; never have to come up in conversation, either in-character or at your table, since in the real world no one really tries to explain luck other than just calling it luck. So too in the Trinity Continuum, Talents may never question their capabilities. It's only organizations like the \u00c6on Society that are trying to research and explain them.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T20:04:14-07:00","id":1454040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1454038#post1454038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I've long maintained that it's difficult to pin down who is and isn't a Talent: they're arguably not a Special Character Type in the way that psions and novas are. They're doing what every other human does subconsciously, they're just better at doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So just like the Psion rules state that a Latent can have one dot in a single Mode, but can only unconsciously activate it at dramatically appropriate times with Storyguide permission, pretty much any normal person could potentially manifest a Gift, but they can't do it on purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T20:52:20-07:00","id":1454048,"title":"","content":"Maybe not a Gift; but I could see, with Storyguide permission, anyone getting a free use of Dramatic Editing. They just wouldn't be able to do it with any sort of consistency. <br /> <br /> In theory, at least. In practice, there's little to distinguish that from the Storyguide just taking it upon himself to alter the narrative in that character's favor. You don't need any game systems to enable this, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T02:58:37-07:00","id":1454060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1454038#post1454038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> FWIW, part of the setting conceit of the Trinity Continuum is that this -- the whole probability manipulation thing -- is <i>how luck actually works</i>. Talents are just better at it than most, but it's not something they're consciously aware of. Like, if you can see a slightly wider range of colour than your friends, you may never notice, and it's not something you try to do, it just happens. There are people who live well into adulthood before finding out they're colourblind. After all, without the ability to compare, most of us are going to assume that our own experiences are universal.<br /> <br /> This is why I've long maintained that it's difficult to pin down who is and isn't a Talent: they're arguably not a Special Character Type in the way that psions and novas are. They're doing what every other human does subconsciously, they're just better at doing it. So the words &amp;quot;flux&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;probability&amp;quot; never have to come up in conversation, either in-character or at your table, since in the real world no one really tries to explain luck other than just calling it luck. So too in the Trinity Continuum, Talents may never question their capabilities. It's only organizations like the \u00c6on Society that are trying to research and explain them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fascinating. That explains a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T05:40:59-07:00","id":1454068,"title":"","content":"There is something on Talents being 'passed along' to the Coalition aliens in Aeon, who started manifesting talents on their own after interacting with the human Talents. This suggests that more than being a genetic byproduct, being a Talent is a contagious state of being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T11:00:12-07:00","id":1454091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1454068#post1454068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is something on Talents being 'passed along' to the Coalition aliens in Aeon, who started manifesting talents on their own after interacting with the human Talents. This suggests that more than being a genetic byproduct, being a Talent is a contagious state of being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give me a page reference for that thing about Talents being infectious?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T11:05:45-07:00","id":1454095,"title":"","content":"Aeon p. 347","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T15:06:49-07:00","id":1454098,"title":"","content":"While I strongly agree in the \u201ccontagious talentness\u201d (makes a lot of sense in both the concept and the idea of once you discover you can do whatever you like you start taking risks and achieve greater deeds), I think the coalition talents are more inspired by the fact that humans can resist the leaders powers and less about interacting with talents. If I am not wrong most of the people kidnapped by coalition (and kept alive) were Psions, teleporters most often, so the number of talents should be closer to 0 than expected in general. But it\u2019s my reading, I am not sure if that\u2019s the inthention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T05:55:09-07:00","id":1454124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1454038#post1454038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FWIW, part of the setting conceit of the Trinity Continuum is that this -- the whole probability manipulation thing -- is <i>how luck actually works</i>. Talents are just better at it than most, but it's not something they're consciously aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, I get how it works &quot;in the Trinity setting&quot;, but I like it as a game mechanic outside the need for &quot;flux&quot;, alternate timelines, etc. The Storypath ruleset with Momentum fueled Dramatic Editing is good for pretty much almost any setting, any &quot;power gimmick&quot;.<br /> <br /> If you want Flux and Flux related powers/science - Trinity Talents are perfect. However, don't want an explanation, just a rules core to build almost anything else - no need for facets, Flux, or societies &quot;explaining&quot; luck, just use the core with Momentum &amp; Dramatic Editing alone. I think it &quot;just works&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T06:04:17-07:00","id":1454125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1454048#post1454048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In theory, at least. In practice, there's little to distinguish that from the Storyguide just taking it upon himself to alter the narrative in that character's favor. You don't need any game systems to enable this, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best/biggest difference between the Storyguide being nice and it requiring some momentum is that Momentum fueled Dramatic Editing provides a &quot;non-favourites&quot; means for the dramatic editing that's in the player's contor. lYou get Momentum from failures and complications. Being able to let the system auto-balance the failures/difficulty with player crafted &quot;success&quot; (or at least opportunities for success) gives the game a neat ludo-narrative system the players can control beyond &quot;just more dice&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T07:11:52-07:00","id":1454130,"title":"","content":"My point was about <i>non-</i>players \u2014 the ones who generally <i>don't</i> use Momentum because they're not really important to the narrative. Technically, anyone is able to access Dramatic Editing; but in practice, only those who are important to the story do so on anything resembling a regular basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T01:08:57-07:00","id":1454264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1454098#post1454098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I strongly agree in the \u201ccontagious talentness\u201d (makes a lot of sense in both the concept and the idea of once you discover you can do whatever you like you start taking risks and achieve greater deeds), I think the coalition talents are more inspired by the fact that humans can resist the leaders powers and less about interacting with talents. If I am not wrong most of the people kidnapped by coalition (and kept alive) were Psions, teleporters most often, so the number of talents should be closer to 0 than expected in general. But it\u2019s my reading, I am not sure if that\u2019s the inthention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the teleporters hadn't come back yet (and the coalition is, fortunately, not teleporting so they haven't got them). Even in a leviathan, most of the crew is going to be humans, and given the high profile of the missions, they tend to send the best of the best humans. So, there is a soft filter for Talents in the crew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T01:21:15-07:00","id":1454265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pcontop</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1454264#post1454264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the teleporters hadn't come back yet (and the coalition is, fortunately, not teleporting so they haven't got them). Even in a leviathan, most of the crew is going to be humans, and given the high profile of the missions, they tend to send the best of the best humans. So, there is a soft filter for Talents in the crew.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right. the ones that got mostly Teleporters was the chromatics, not the coalition\u2026 yes, probably a lot of Talents in the Leviathans for sure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T13:29:04-07:00","id":1464532,"title":"","content":"The core book supports having &quot;Talent&quot; player characters who are actually just that good Baseline characters, I believe. It's just a narrative thing, mechanically the character would play the same as a Talent. I'm not sure how that would work with the Gift that lets you pick out people who have access to a Source power. Could it be used to game the system and give yourself stealth powers that other people can't detect when you use them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T17:56:24-07:00","id":1464544,"title":"","content":"Nobody, except a very small number of talents can detect other talents, so if you wish you can just consider you talent as a amazing baseline.<br /> <br /> The thing about Talents is that they are not really powered, they are just awesome, be it by luck, skill or intention. Flux is the \u201cscientific\u201d explanation, but no even talents really understand they are bringing stuff from other realities. From their point of view things were always that way and they are just luck it is that way.<br /> <br /> About Talents detecting Talents, they would detect them as capable of doing weird things. It\u2019s not like a Nova that can detect powers and other novas, capable of quantifying that somehow, or as a Psion that sense novas as a lack of psi, and can detect all kind of things with their powers. Talents just feel a general weirdness in other talents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T18:34:54-07:00","id":1464546,"title":"","content":"Talents get access to the &quot;Behold the Halo&quot; Gift that allows them to know the Source type and rating of every nearby person. It probably manifests as a gut feeling, but as written it seems to mean that Talents with this Gift can detect Talents, Psi users and Quantum users. Seems like a pretty powerful ability only limited in how much faith you're willing to put in someone's gut feeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T06:02:36-07:00","id":1464582,"title":"","content":"Random question<br /> <br /> Is the Inspiration mechanic in D&amp;D 5e borrowed from Trinity Continuum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T14:46:11-07:00","id":1464643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1464582#post1464582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random question<br /> <br /> Is the Inspiration mechanic in D&amp;D 5e borrowed from Trinity Continuum?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think so. It\u2019s more like momentum/action points than inspiration from Adventure/TC","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T22:05:34-07:00","id":1464691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1198028-talented-baselines?p=1464643#post1464643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t think so. It\u2019s more like momentum/action points than inspiration from Adventure/TC</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}